  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{x-7}-4\\,?$\n\nThe range is\n$f(x)\\in (-\\infty \\,,$\n{{field-1}}$)\u22c3($\n{{field-2}}\n$,$\n{{field-3}}$).$",
  "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=-4.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-4,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\u22c3(-4,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/assets/b0dc57e0ce542dd61afc7bd114830a0c82b74a25a8c1befff3b6e4de5c8eb8f5.png)",
